  "description": "The 26\" OM Flyer is a bike with some serious history. The \"OM\" in the name stands for \"Old Man,\" which was the nickname of SE Bikes founder, Scot Breithaupt. It's a bike that pays homage to a true legend and pioneer in BMX, but is also ready to be ridden at today’s level of riding. The 100% Cr-Mo frame is a pure classic, giving you the feel of a real steel BMX bike. The unique SE Mohawk flip flop hubs and double-wall rims roll on 26 x 2.4\" Bozack tires, which provide a ride that is as smooth as it gets. And the new Scot Enterprises top-load stem adds a touch of retro flair, while the Oakley B-1B grips give the bike an added touch of awesome authenticity.",
